ommit_sha":"7edde0a5c12baaef528e8f19978cc71f104419b0","position":"1785517237064775698-6b256b60-37a7-40af-b6aa-4cd3c2255c99"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"3e8a6e8c9d1d15c612b4cdbd0b607174a680ca16f4041c6889fa330c3dfaa533","event_uuid":"8a3972b3-1372-4b50-93a4-c93da69adf5e","position":{"commit_sha":"9ac2c9782299dc3545a009eb821562aa58334f9f","position":"1785521938023703001-8a3972b3-1372-4b50-93a4-c93da69adf5e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"0411de2b8b32de6c7ae1b7ed12c0b7a83f120e99fa7e543f9755621699c6d282","event_uuid":"de91389c-b0e2-407d-be51-e0a2dc9a0ecb","position":{"commit_sha":"e330700759e5d01dd531244afbae8598cd25d8e8","position":"1785527034738378001-de91389c-b0e2-407d-be51-e0a2dc9a0ecb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-220_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"52d5d6e0-1933-4be1-9d52-bba891ba7553","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Candidate field occurrence from a cross-source log audit (2026-07-30) — offered as a lead, explicitly NOT as proof.\n\nThis bug describes `materialize/_materialize_tree` being able to lazy-fetch unboundedly on a partial clone with no `run_git` timeout. There is exactly one production event in the retained journald history (2026-07-03 -> today) whose shape matches an unbounded fetch/clone: the review bot's only per-review timeout, on the Gerrit host `i-00880b2c7f13527c5`:\n\n    2026-07-13T08:22:05Z  VOTER_ERROR {\"event\": \"VOTER_ERROR\",\n      \"timestamp\": 1783930925.7817554,\n      \"change_id\": \"I0cbe64257ac6d593dc0e024cfb875c62abcdf611\",\n      \"revision_id\": null, \"vote_value\": null, \"http_status\": null,\n      \"error\": \"review timed out after 1200.0s — abandoned to keep the queue draining\n                (hung clone/subprocess/LLM); the backfill reconciler will retry\"}\n\nRelevant details:\n- It is the ONLY `review timed out after` event in the whole retained journal (verified: `journalctl --since 2026-07-03 | grep -c \"review timed out after\"` = 1), and the last `VOTER_ERROR` of any kind on record.\n- The review hung for the full 1200s ceiling — i.e. it did not fail, it made no progress until the outer watchdog killed it. That is the signature an untimed `run_git` fetch would produce.\n- The bot's own message names \"hung clone\" first among the suspects.\n\nWhat I could NOT establish: the message is a generic catch-all emitted by the outer `asyncio.wait_for` watchdog, so it does not identify which subprocess hung. I have no stack, no git trace, and no evidence tying it to `_materialize_tree` specifically rather than to a subprocess or LLM call. The 1200s watchdog (from 9d7c / 89be) is what caught it, and it self-healed via the backfill reconciler.\n\nUse: if a timeout is added to `run_git` under this ticket, this event is a concrete pre-fix datapoint to cite, and its non-recurrence afterwards would be weak-but-real evidence. Do not treat it as a confirmed reproduction.","timestamp":1785451671066980001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"--body","timestamp":1785516826958529001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"--body","timestamp":1785521938023703001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"--body","timestamp":1785527034738378001}],"created_at":1785006820619764001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f574eed3-c3ea-4332-bc8c-ad3d4c1b9d87","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"72d9-8fbd-3a9e-48a6"},{"link_uuid":"b30b5879-50da-4b19-a741-db9abd11081f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2aae-789a-282a-4a8e"}],"description":"Found during the 72d9 CI-hang investigation (faulthandler-proven). Mechanism: _fetch_origin prefers a blobless partial fetch (--filter=blob:none, src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py fetch site). On a checkout that is itself shallow (CI: git init + fetch --depth=1), materialize_tickets/materialize can therefore resolve a ref whose blobs are absent, and _materialize_tree's git read-tree / git checkout-index --all (repo_snapshot.py:447-461) then triggers git's promisor lazy fetching — one HTTPS round trip per missing object batch — with no timeout anywhere (run_git's timeout parameter defaults to None and no caller passes one). Observed: a single checkout-index blocked >15 minutes per test and hours per CI lane. A production rebar MCP server running from a shallow or partial clone can hang the same way. Expected: local-looking materialization must fail fast (or fetch missing objects in ONE batched, bounded operation) instead of unbounded lazy fetching. Suggested directions: set GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH=1 (git >= 2.43) in _materialize_tree's env so a missing object errors immediately with an actionable message; and/or pass explicit timeouts on network-capable run_git call sites; and/or detect a shallow/promisor repo in acquire() and surface a descriptive SnapshotError. Acceptance criteria: (1) materializing a tree whose blobs are absent from a partial clone fails within seconds with a descriptive error naming the remedy, pinned by a unit test using a --filter=blob:none clone fixture; (2) no run_git call on the materialize path can block indefinitely (timeout or GIT_NO_LAZY_FETCH), asserted by test; (3) make lint, make typecheck, and the default suite exit zero.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","2aae-789a-282a-4a8e"]],"parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"de943e09-507f-417e-b279-4d472facf933","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"747f-d1ba-dd43-43f4","ticket_type":"bug","title":"materialize/_materialize_tree can lazy-fetch unboundedly on a partial clone (no run_git timeout): local-looking git ops hang for hours","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["653899b6-40ec-4e65-9ebf-8103bc497de0","f574eed3-c3ea-4332-bc8c-ad3d4c1b9d87","925ef969-542c-43ad-9cca-40532ff34179","de943e09-507f-417e-b279-4d472facf933","35895143-c2a1-4e1e-8698-0e095c0ff59b","99a22dc4-90aa-4822-b709-aaff92d67c52","6b256b60-37a7-40af-b6aa-4cd3c2255c99","8a3972b3-1372-4b50-93a4-c93da69adf5e","b30b5879-50da-4b19-a741-db9abd11081f","de91389c-b0e2-407d-be51-e0a2dc9a0ecb"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785527034738378002,"uuid":"6b6e1191-4fe1-4aaa-b006-9c24ef995dac"}